# runtime.Dedicated, Thread and Joined.Join: a dedicated Io's tasks share one
# carrier thread and never overlap, a Thread's f and its tasks end before Join returns, and a Join
# in a cancelled scope is Canceled with the Joined kept. Both profiles, both targets; the output
# is the same at MK_CARRIERS=1 and 16 (linux.sh runs both on Linux).
case ok
stdout threads.out
